# rule.always.scope-onetime-lessons-to-the-behavior

a lesson born inside a behavior has **two homes**; most incidents need both, linked.

| tier | home | holds |
|---|---|---|
| one-time | `$behavior/` | instance-bound result, with evidence |
| durable | `.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/`, or another repo via radio | repo-agnostic kernel |

1. scope the instance (files, diffs, commands, failures) into `$behavior/`
2. always ask *"what is the durable kernel?"*; distill it
3. link both ways: durable brief says *"first seen in `<repo>/$behavior/<slug>`"*; behavior doc points up

a lesson whose home is another repo is re-seeded there, never adopted here.

test: useful only to someone who ran this behavior → behavior dir · to a traveler in any repo → durable brief, linked back · both (common) → two writes.

blocker: an instance-bound lesson in the durable dir · a durable kernel discarded with its behavior dir · another repo's lesson adopted here.
nitpick: a durable brief with no worked-example citation · a behavior doc with no pointer up.
